From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] appxpackaging: The package writer (6056)

IAppxFactory::CreatePackageWriter gave E_NOTIMPL. Packaging tools
(MSIX packagers, build systems, installers that repackage) write AppX and
MSIX packages with it.

IAppxPackageWriter is declared in appxpackaging.idl. New writer.c writes
the ZIP as files are added: each payload file's local header and data,
deflated with a full flush after every 64 KiB so each block's compressed
size goes in the block map; Close adds AppxManifest.xml (refused unless
the manifest reader takes it), AppxBlockMap.xml with every block's hash,
[Content_Types].xml and the central directory, with ZIP64 records where
32 bits do not do (unless the settings force ZIP32). Names are stored as
OPC part names; repeated and footprint names are refused.
---
